`lib/WWW/Bund/Caller.pm:152-157` puts the value of the env var named by `auth_env` into the query string (`share/endpoints.yml:557` uses it for `ladestationen` with `LADESTATIONEN_TOKEN`). The full URL including `?token=...` is then

- logged at debug (`$log->debug("$method $url ...")`), at info on success (line 216) and at error on failure (line 212),
- put into the exception: `croak "Bund API error: HTTP ... for $method $url"` (line 213), which the CLI prints,
- used as the cache key (line 184; only its MD5 reaches the disk, so that part is harmless).

A rejected or expired token is the typical case in which the error path runs, and it prints that token.

Done when: the URL used for log lines and error messages has the `auth_query_param` value masked (e.g. `token=***`), and `t/caller.t` asserts that neither the croak message nor the captured log contains the token.

